@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s47a-definitions`
IMPORT `ito-s45a-insurance-and-pension-credit`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 47(b)-(d) — the deduction for payments to a pension provident fund.
-- Row IL-08. Source lines 1778-1789.
--
-- GAPS.md item 1 of row IL-07 names s 47 with s 45A. The definitions of s 47(a) are encoded first,
-- in ito-s47a-definitions.l4, because s 45A borrows them; this module is the deduction itself, taken
-- in GAPS order after the row's own list.
--
-- (b): an individual who is NOT a beneficiary member deducts sums paid to a pension provident fund
-- only (or to keep a pension right), up to limits by income: limb (1) on qualifying income that is
-- not work income, limb (2) on work income that is not insured income. (b1): a beneficiary member
-- deducts sums paid for himself (or a child of 18 or more), up to 11% of his income for a
-- self-employed member, and then up to 7% (with a further 4% above 12%) of his additional income.
-- (b2) forbids deducting a sum twice; (c) keeps a deducted sum out of s 45A (applied there); (d)
-- empowers the Minister to set higher rates, and regulations of 5740-1980 were made.
--
-- For an employee whose whole salary is insured income, every limit here is nil: an employee's own
-- contributions go to the s 45A credit, not to this deduction (tests).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 47(b)-(d) — the deduction`

§§ `(b) — an individual who is not a beneficiary member`

-- src:1778 | (ב) יחיד שאינו עמית מוטב, שבשנת המס שילמו הוא או בן זוגו סכומים לקופת גמל לקצבה בלבד, לטובת אחד מהם, והכל, גם אם ציווה שלאחר מותו תועבר זכותו לטובת מוסד שהוכר כמוסד ציבורי לענין סעיף 9(2), או ששילמו כאמור למדינה, לרשות מקומית או לגוף אחר שקבע שר האוצר, לשם שמירת זכות הפנסיה של אחד מהם, יותר ניכוי הסכומים ששולמו כאמור ובלבד שהניכוי לא יעלה על –
-- src:1779 | (1) 7% מהכנסתו המזכה שאיננה הכנסת עבודה; ואולם אם שילם סכום העולה על 12% מהכנסתו כאמור, יותר לו, בשל החלק העולה על 12% כאמור, ניכוי נוסף עד ל־4% מאותה הכנסה;
-- src:1780 | (2) הסכום הנמוך מבין אלה:
-- src:1781 | (א) 5% מהכנסתו המזכה שהיא הכנסת עבודה שאינה הכנסה מבוטחת;
-- src:1782 | (ב) 5% מהכנסתו החייבת שהיא הכנסת עבודה עד לסכום השווה לשתי פעמים וחצי הסכום האמור בפסקה (1) להגדרה ”הכנסה מזכה“ לשנה, בניכוי הכנסתו המבוטחת.

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i MEANS
         i's `sums paid, for section 47`'s `to a pension provident fund only, by the individual or the spouse, for the benefit of one of them`
    PLUS i's `sums paid, for section 47`'s `to the State, a local authority or a designated body, to keep the pension right of one of them`

-- Limb (1): 7% of the qualifying income that is not work income, and where more than 12% of it was
-- paid, a further deduction for the part above 12%, of up to 4% of it.
@ref ITO s 47(b)(1), line 1779
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b)(1) — the limit on qualifying income that is not work income, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    7% TIMES `the income` PLUS min (4% TIMES `the income`) (max 0 (`s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i MINUS 12% TIMES `the income`))
    WHERE `the income` MEANS `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is not work income:` i `,` a

-- Limb (2): the lower of 5% of the qualifying work income that is not insured income (insured income
-- read as taken into the qualifying work income first, fork F6), and 5% of the taxable work income up
-- to two and a half times the paragraph (1) amount, less the insured income.
@ref ITO s 47(b)(2), lines 1780-1782
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b)(2) — the limit on work income that is not insured income, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    min (5% TIMES max 0 (`s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is work income:` i `,` a MINUS i's `insured income`))
        (5% TIMES max 0 (min (i's `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`)
                             (2.5 TIMES a's `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income`)
                         MINUS i's `insured income`))

-- "ובלבד שהניכוי לא יעלה על – (1) ...; (2) ...": the two limbs measure two different kinds of income,
-- and are read as adding up (fork F27).
@ref ITO s 47(b), lines 1778-1782
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` i `, at` a
    THEN 0
    ELSE min (`s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i)
             (`s 47(b)(1) — the limit on qualifying income that is not work income, for` i `, at` a
              PLUS `s 47(b)(2) — the limit on work income that is not insured income, for` i `, at` a)

§§ `(b1) — a beneficiary member`

-- src:1783 | (ב1) לעמית מוטב שבשנת המס שילמו הוא או בן זוגו סכומים לקופת גמל לקצבה לטובת העמית המוטב, ולעמית מוטב שבשנת המס שילם סכומים כאמור לטובת ילדו שגילו, בשנת המס, 18 שנים ומעלה, יותר ניכוי הסכומים ששולמו כאמור, ובלבד שהניכוי לא יעלה על אלה, לפי הענין:
-- src:1784 | (1) בשל סכומים ששולמו כאמור – 11% מההכנסה לעמית עצמאי;
-- src:1785 | (2) בשל סכומים ששולמו כאמור ושבשלם לא הותר ניכוי לפי פסקה (1) – 7% מההכנסה הנוספת; ואולם אם הסכומים ששולמו כאמור עולים על 12% מהכנסתו הנוספת, יותר לו בשל החלק העולה על 12% כאמור, ניכוי נוסף שלא יעלה על 4% מההכנסה הנוספת, והכל בלבד שלא יינתן ניכוי לפי פסקה זו בשל סכומים שהופקדו בעד העמית המוטב שסכומם אינו עולה על 16% מהשכר הממוצע במשק.

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i MEANS
         i's `sums paid, for section 47`'s `to a pension provident fund, by the individual or the spouse, for the benefit of the beneficiary member`
    PLUS i's `sums paid, for section 47`'s `to a pension provident fund, by the beneficiary member, for the benefit of a child aged 18 or more`

@ref ITO s 47(b1)(1), line 1784
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1)(1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    min (`s 47(b1) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i)
        (11% TIMES `s 47(a)(3) — the income for a self-employed member of` i `, at` a)

-- (2)'s proviso: no deduction under (2) "for sums deposited for the beneficiary member whose amount
-- does not exceed 16% of the average wage". Read (fork F29) as: of all the sums deposited for him in
-- the year (the figure that made him a beneficiary member, s 47(a)(7)), the first 16% of the average
-- wage summed over the year earns no deduction under (2); so (2) can reach only the part of the sums
-- not deducted under (1) that lies above that.
@ref ITO s 47(b1)(2), proviso, line 1785
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1)(2) — the sums paragraph (2) can reach, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    min (`s 47(b1) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i MINUS `s 47(b1)(1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a)
        (max 0 (i's `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income`
                MINUS `s 47(a)(7) — the least sum that makes a beneficiary member, at` a))

GIVEN `the sums`            IS A NUMBER
      `the additional income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1)(2) — the limit, where the sums tested against 12% are` `the sums` `and the additional income is` `the additional income` MEANS
    7% TIMES `the additional income`
    PLUS min (4% TIMES `the additional income`) (max 0 (`the sums` MINUS 12% TIMES `the additional income`))

@ref ITO s 47(b1)(2): the 12% test may be read on the sums not deducted under (1) or on those the proviso leaves
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 47(b1)(2) does not say whether its 12% test counts the sums its proviso excludes` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 47(b1)(2) does not say whether its 12% test counts the sums its proviso excludes"

-- "אם הסכומים ששולמו כאמור עולים על 12% מהכנסתו הנוספת": "the sums paid as aforesaid" may be every sum
-- not deducted under (1), or only those the proviso lets (2) reach. Where the two readings give
-- different limits the rule declines (fork F30); usually they agree.
@ref ITO s 47(b1)(2), line 1785
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1)(2) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `on all` EQUALS `on the reachable`
    THEN `on all`
    ELSE `section 47(b1)(2) does not say whether its 12% test counts the sums its proviso excludes`
    WHERE
        `additional income` MEANS `s 47(a)(5) — the additional income of` i `, at` a
        `not under (1)`     MEANS `s 47(b1) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i MINUS `s 47(b1)(1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a
        `reachable`         MEANS `s 47(b1)(2) — the sums paragraph (2) can reach, for` i `, at` a
        `on all`            MEANS min `reachable` (`s 47(b1)(2) — the limit, where the sums tested against 12% are` `not under (1)` `and the additional income is` `additional income`)
        `on the reachable`  MEANS min `reachable` (`s 47(b1)(2) — the limit, where the sums tested against 12% are` `reachable` `and the additional income is` `additional income`)

@ref ITO s 47(b1), lines 1783-1785
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47(b1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` i `, at` a
    THEN `s 47(b1)(1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a PLUS `s 47(b1)(2) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a
    ELSE 0

§§ `(b2), (c), (d)`

-- src:1786 | (ב2) סכום שנוכה לפי סעיף קטן (ב), לא יהיה ניתן לנכותו לפי סעיף קטן (ב1), ולהיפך.
-- By construction: (b) applies only to one who is not a beneficiary member and (b1) only to one who
-- is, so no individual has both in one year; and the two take their sums from different fields.
-- src:1787 | (ג) סכום שנוכה לפי סעיף קטן (ב) או (ב1) לא יובא בחשבון לצורך סעיף 45א.
-- Applied in ito-s45a-insurance-and-pension-credit.l4, which takes the sums deducted as an input.
-- (0.4.0) Which of the two takes a payment first is fork F35, below.
-- src:1788 | (ד) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע ניכויים בשיעורים גבוהים מהאמורים בסעיף קטן (ב) לסוג מסויים של בני־אדם ובתנאים ובסייגים שיקבע.
-- src:1789 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (ניכוי תשלומים בעד תגמולים או קיצבה), תש״ם–1980.]
@ref ITO s 47(d), lines 1788-1789 — the regulations of 5740-1980 are not in the source bundle
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the regulations under section 47(d) are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "the regulations under section 47(d) are not encoded in this model"

§§ `The order of the deduction and the section 45A credit (fork F35; version 0.4.0)`

-- One payment to a pension fund may be deducted here or credited under s 45A, not both: (c) keeps a
-- deducted sum out of s 45A. Neither section says which takes the payment first. Versions 0.1.0 to
-- 0.3.0 took the deduction first, always the largest deduction s 47 allows (the independent pass's
-- D190, D236; inventory 08i-D190). RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG): one named switch (nouns,
-- `A reading of the order between the deduction under section 47 and the credit under section 45A`),
-- every reading kept by name and tested, and by default a refusal where the order changes the answer.
--   the deduction first: the deduction (b) or (b1) allows, out of the sums paid.
--   the credit first: s 45A credits first, as far as its limits allow, with nothing deducted; the
--     deduction then takes what is left, up to the same limits. The limits are those of the sums he
--     paid ("אם שילם סכום העולה על 12%" is about what he paid, whichever takes it first); only the sums
--     the deduction can take are fewer. So it is the lesser of the deduction first and the sums paid
--     less the pension sums s 45A credits.
--   the order the taxpayer chooses: one of the two, as he states.
--   declined where the order changes the answer (the default): where the two orders give the same
--     deduction, that deduction; otherwise a refusal by name. They give the same where s 47 allows
--     nothing, and where the sums paid cover both the credit's and the deduction's limits.
-- Worked: D190, self-employed, not a beneficiary member, 100,000 of income, 10,000 paid. Deduction
-- first: 7% of 100,000 = 7,000 (10,000 is not above 12%), the credit then on 3,000. Credit first:
-- s 45A(d)(2)(b)(1) credits 5% of 100,000 = 5,000; the deduction takes 10,000 - 5,000 = 5,000. The
-- orders differ: declined by default. With 20,000 paid: 11,000 either way (20,000 - 5,000 = 15,000
-- leaves room for all 11,000).
@ref ITO s 47(b), (b1), (c), lines 1778-1787; s 45A; fork F35; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of the order between the deduction under section 47 and the credit under section 45A`
`section 47 — the reading this row takes of the order between the deduction and the section 45A credit` MEANS
    `declined where the order changes the answer`

@ref ITO s 47(c), line 1787; s 45A; fork F35
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"

-- The individual with nothing deducted, for s 45A to credit first.
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`s 47 — the individual with nothing deducted under section 47:` i MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS i's `tax year`
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS i's `an Israeli resident in the tax year`
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS i's `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS i's `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS i's `taxable income from a business or profession`
        `insured income`                                                                IS i's `insured income`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS i's `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS i's `sums paid, for section 45A`
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS i's `sums paid, for section 47`
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS i's `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)`
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS i's `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`   IS i's `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`
        `a foreign worker`                                                              IS i's `a foreign worker`

-- The pension sums (s 45A(b)'s first two limbs, and (b1)'s for a child) that s 45A credits with
-- nothing deducted. Where nothing is cut, all of them. Where its limits cut, and they are the only
-- creditable sums, the sums its 35% rule credits. Where they cut sums of other kinds too (life or
-- survivors' insurance), which are credited s 45A does not say (fork F1): declined, in its words.
-- s 48A may take the credit from a foreign worker: declined where it would credit any of these.
@ref ITO s 45A(b), (b1), (d), (e), lines 1718-1738; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 and s 45A — the pension sums section 45A credits with nothing deducted, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   i's `a foreign worker` AND `the credited sums` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `row IL-08: section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded`
    ELSE `the credited sums`
    WHERE
        i0                 MEANS `s 47 — the individual with nothing deducted under section 47:` i
        `the limit`        MEANS `s 45A(d)-(e) — the limit that governs, for` i0 `, at` a
        `the most`         MEANS `s 45A(d)-(e) — the most for which credit is given, under` `the limit`
        `limb (1) governs` MEANS `the limit`'s `the fixed amount of limb (1)` AT LEAST `the limit`'s `the amount of limb (2)`
        `at 25%`           MEANS `s 45A — the sums that may be credited at 25%, for` i0 `, at` a
        `at 35%`           MEANS `s 45A — the sums that may be credited at 35%, for` i0 `, at` a
        `pension`          MEANS `s 45A(b) — the pension sums that may be credited, for` i0
                                 PLUS `s 45A(b1) — the child's pension sums that may be credited, for` i0 `, at` a
        `survivors`        MEANS `s 45A(b) — the survivors' pension insurance sums that may be credited, for` i0
        `the credited sums` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF   `at 25%` PLUS `at 35%` AT MOST `the most`
                     AND (`limb (1) governs` OR `the limit`'s `the sums as paid are within the provisos of limb (2)`)
                THEN `pension`
                IF   `at 25%` EQUALS 0 AND `survivors` EQUALS 0
                THEN `s 45A(d)-(e) — the sums credited, where every creditable sum is at 35%, for` i0 `, at` a
                OTHERWISE `section 45A does not say which sums are credited when its limits cut sums of different kinds`

-- The sums s 47 can take: (b)'s for one who is not a beneficiary member, (b1)'s for one who is.
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 — the sums the deduction can take, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` i `, at` a
    THEN `s 47(b1) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i
    ELSE `s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i

@ref ITO s 47(b), (b1), lines 1778-1785
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 — the deduction, the deduction taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    `s 47(b) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a PLUS `s 47(b1) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a

@ref ITO s 47(b), (b1), (c), lines 1778-1787; s 45A
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 — the deduction, the section 45A credit taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `first` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `first`
             (max 0 (`s 47 — the sums the deduction can take, for` i `, at` a
                     MINUS `s 47 and s 45A — the pension sums section 45A credits with nothing deducted, for` i `, at` a))
    WHERE `first` MEANS `s 47 — the deduction, the deduction taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a

@ref ITO s 47(b)-(d), lines 1778-1789; fork F35
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
      r IS A `A reading of the order between the deduction under section 47 and the credit under section 45A`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47 for` i `, at` a `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as` r MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-08 answers`
        (IF   i's `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`
         THEN `the regulations under section 47(d) are not encoded in this model`
         ELSE CONSIDER r
              WHEN `the deduction first` THEN `deduction first`
              WHEN `the credit first`    THEN `credit first`
              WHEN `the order the taxpayer chooses` `deduction first chosen`
                  THEN IF `deduction first chosen` THEN `deduction first` ELSE `credit first`
              WHEN `declined where the order changes the answer`
                  THEN IF   `deduction first` EQUALS `credit first`
                       THEN `deduction first`
                       ELSE `sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer`)
    WHERE
        `deduction first` MEANS `s 47 — the deduction, the deduction taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a
        `credit first`    MEANS `s 47 — the deduction, the section 45A credit taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a

-- Versions 0.1.0 to 0.3.0's entry point, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names (the
-- default: declined where the order changes the answer). The independent tests and row IL-07's
-- capstone call it.
@export The deduction from income, in NIS for a tax year from 2024, under Income Tax Ordinance s 47(b) or (b1) for payments to a pension provident fund (s 47 is a deduction, not a credit); declines where the order between the deduction and the s 45A credit for the same payment changes the answer (fork F35, Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08)
@ref ITO s 47(b)-(d), lines 1778-1789; fork F35
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
          @desc the individual, the tax year, the income split into work and other income, the insured income, the sums deposited for him, the sums paid by limb of s 47(b) and (b1), and the sums paid by limb of s 45A (the credit the same payments may take)
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
          @desc NIS; the s 45A(d)(1) amount, the two s 47(a)(1) amounts as adjusted under s 120B for the tax year, and the National Insurance average wage summed over the tax year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47 for` i `, at` a MEANS
    `the deduction under section 47 for` i `, at` a `, reading the order with the section 45A credit as`
        `section 47 — the reading this row takes of the order between the deduction and the section 45A credit`
